BT /F2 12 Tf 0 g 72 572.70 Td (Abstract) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 0 g 72 551.91 Td (Defines clinical outcome prediction tasks from admission notes \(diagnoses, procedures,) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 0 g 72 537.42 Td (in-hospital mortality, length of stay\) and proposes clinical outcome pre-training that) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 0 g 72 522.93 Td (integrates knowledge from multiple sources.) Tj ET
BT /F2 12 Tf 0 g 72 488.37 Td (1 Introduction) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 0 g 72 467.58 Td (Neural language models have become the default tool for a wide range of text) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 0 g 72 453.09 Td (understanding problems. This question has become central as models are deployed on longer) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 0 g 72 438.60 Td (and more heterogeneous inputs, and as practitioners weigh accuracy against cost.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 0 g 72 417.81 Td (Clinical notes differ from general-domain text in vocabulary, abbreviation density, and) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 0 g 72 403.32 Td (document length; a typical discharge summary in MIMIC-III exceeds 1,500 word pieces, far) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 0 g 72 388.83 Td (beyond the 512-token window of standard encoders.) Tj ET
BT /F2 12 Tf 0 g 72 354.27 Td (2 Related Work) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 0 g 72 333.48 Td (Prior work spans architectural changes to the attention mechanism, training objectives) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 0 g 72 318.99 Td (tailored to the target domain, and evaluation suites that probe robustness. We review the) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 0 g 72 304.50 Td (most closely related approaches and highlight where our assumptions differ.) Tj ET
BT /F2 12 Tf 0 g 72 269.94 Td (3 Method) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 0 g 72 249.15 Td (We describe the model architecture, the training objective and the optimization schedule,) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 0 g 72 234.66 Td (and note where our choices depart from common practice. We stratify performance by note) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 0 g 72 220.17 Td (type \(discharge summary, radiology, nursing\) and by patient subgroups to assess whether) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 0 g 72 205.68 Td (gains are uniform across the population.) Tj ET
BT /F2 12 Tf 0 g 72 171.12 Td (4 Experiments) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 0 g 72 150.33 Td (All data were accessed under the PhysioNet credentialed data use agreement. Protected) Tj ET
